      "side": 1,
      "message": "I may be missing a case here: with `mm_is_p3s_4k()` in this condition, removing a probe from a 4KB process never zaps the restored page, so the probed page stays a private anonymous copy, while native processes go back to the page cache page. The commit message doesn\u0027t mention this.\n\nAs far as I can see, the zap would also work in a 4KB VMA: `orig_page_is_identical()` finds the file page through `vaddr_to_offset()` and compares the whole 16KB page, which `wp_page_copy()` copied in full; the zap only drops this slice PTE; and `collapse_pte_mapped_thp()` bails out, since `vma_thp_disabled()` is true for 4KB VMAs.\n\nIf 4KB processes do need to keep the copy, could the commit message (or a comment) say why, and could the check use `vma_is_p3s_4k(vma)`, like the one above?",
      "isAi": true,
